# No em dash or en dash

Do not use em dashes (U+2014) or en dashes (U+2013) anywhere in this project.

This applies to:

- User-facing copy (UI labels, titles, messages, placeholders)
- Code comments and docstrings
- README and documentation
- SEO/meta titles and descriptions
- Commit messages and PR text when working in this repo

## Use instead

| Instead of | Use |
|------------|-----|
| Em dash in titles | Pipe or hyphen: `Page \| App` or `Page - App` |
| Em dash in prose | Comma, colon, or hyphen: `foo: bar` or `foo - bar` |
| En dash in ranges | Hyphen or words: `1-10` or `1 to 10` |
| Em dash as empty placeholder | `N/A`, `-`, or `None` |

Regular ASCII hyphen-minus (`-`, U+002D) is allowed.

## Examples

```text
// BAD (uses U+2014 em dash)
Sign in [em dash] Manufacturer Panel
// Server state is authoritative [em dash] mock data for now

// BAD (uses U+2013 en dash)
Showing 1[en dash]10 of 50

// GOOD
Sign in | Manufacturer Panel
Showing 1-10 of 50
// Server state is authoritative; mock data for now
```

When editing existing text, replace em/en dashes rather than introducing new ones.
